web888-redpitaya (2025.430-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Hardware-gate fix: patch 0001-peri-use-zynqsdr-ioctl —
    sdr_receiver_hpsdr's peri.c drove the PE4312 DSA via sysfs GPIO
    523/525/524, but the zynqsdr kernel driver owns MIO 11/12/13 on this
    image (EBUSY → vendor code dereferenced a NULL FILE* and SEGV'd).
    peri.c now uses the driver's ZYNQSDR_AD8370_SET ioctl (step-2
    hw-gate proven, PL-bitstream-agnostic) and returns -1 on failure
    instead of crashing.
  * web888-rpapp@.service: + StartLimitIntervalSec=120 StartLimitBurst=10 —
    a hardware-gate SEGV crash-loop reloaded the bitstream every ~4s for ~15min
    (sustained devcfg churn, device later found hung); cap restarts so a
    failing app gives up instead of churning the PL.

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 01:30:00 +0800

web888-redpitaya (2025.430-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package of the Web-888 Red Pitaya app stack
    (step 4, Red Pitaya coexistence):
    - C servers built from source: RaspSDR/red-pitaya-notes @ da1a7e3a
      (2025-04-30, MIT): sdr-receiver, sdr-receiver-hpsdr,
      sdr-transceiver-wide; si5351-init from scripts/hw-test/si5351.
    - Vendored factory bitstreams (Vivado 2023.1, 2024/12): led_blinker,
      sdr_receiver, sdr_receiver_hpsdr, sdr_transceiver_wide
      (/usr/share/web888-redpitaya/apps/<app>/<app>.bit).
    - web888-rpapp@.service template: root (required for /dev/mem),
      bitstream load in ExecStartPre via load-bitstream (prog_done
      poll, fail closed), Conflicts=web888-websdr.service; drop-in
      50-redpitaya.conf declares the reverse conflict on the websdr
      unit. No [Install] — never auto-enabled.
    - /usr/sbin/web888-mode runtime switch (websdr/<app>/stop/list).
    - /etc/web888-redpitaya/switch.conf conffile: SI5351_RESET=0
      default until hardware measurement settles the requirement.

